# Operational, machine-local artefacts — NOT code (owner via coordinator seq2954). Added after the
# operational dirs kept turning up as untracked and one `git add -A` would have swept them into a
# commit: the same hazard that caught three foreign files in the tradingadvisor tree today.
logs/
start_agents.log
state/
relay.yaml.bak.*

# state/deepcode_resume.uuid stays TRACKED on purpose: gitignore does not affect already-tracked
# files, and that file is the session's resume pointer. Consequence, stated rather than hidden: a
# FUTURE state file that must be versioned will not appear in `git status` — it needs `git add -f` or
# an explicit negation. I chose hiding the operational noise over the risk of silently losing a
# pointer on a fresh clone, because the pointer is the thing nobody can regenerate by hand.
